        "original_id": "4def0dcd-2663-57e8-96b3-0353e2fe0d07",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Kazanjian, Harry Kizirian, Chris Enss\n- Organizations: Lucasfilm, United States Marine Corps\n- Works: Raiders of the Lost Ark, Return of the Jedi, books about Roy Rogers and Dale Evans\n- Topics: film production, World War II, women in the Old West\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Kizirian was born on July 13, 1925, and he later served in the United States Marine Corps during World War II.\n- Howard G. Kazanjian was born on July 26, 1942, and he became an American film producer.\n- Howard Kazanjian is known for the films \"Raiders of the Lost Ark\" and \"Return of the Jedi.\"\n- Howard Kazanjian served for eight years as a Vice President of Lucasfilm, Ltd.\n- Howard Kazanjian is also a published non-fiction author.\n- Harry Kizirian was an Armenian American.\n- Harry Kizirian died on September 13, 2002.\n- Chris Enss has written more than 20 books about women in the Old West.\n- Chris Enss collaborated with producer Howard Kazanjian on four books, including two about Roy Rogers and Dale Evans.",
